  "contracts": [
    "Exact supplied catalog generation and recovery checksums; host owns catalog-store acceptance and selection.",
    "Private owner and original seed preserved. Catalog PublisherID preserves fact lineage; scheduler, origin, and serving permission stay independent.",
    "Pending or incomplete materialization refuses runtime startup. Changed request, current inputs, continuity, or native target refuses retry.",
    "Completed exact retry returns immutable receipt without replacing later state. Missing active selection refuses startup but completed retry never recreates it.",
    "New explicit operation can bind a separately restored owner/seed-verified directory; prior native receipts remain unchanged history. Automatic startup and old-operation retry reject the copied target.",
    "Retains every supplied historical capsule, manual input checkpoint, original removals and accepted pin. Explicit historical baseline survives newer embedded binary and later semantic input capture.",
    "No acquisition, provider/source reads, lease acquisition, clock callback, or serving permission issuance. Configured external role probes remain unused.",
    "Private native record publication and real process-exit recovery tested at plan, selection, and baseline publication points.",
    "Precise runtime file-inspection patterns retain reviewed generation-input/baseline repair and new materialization records; unknown files remain rejected and unchanged."
